-- title:
--   From HTo GAdjacent Stage M1 Eq Half Sandwich Left Shape
-- statement:
--   **$M_1$ equals its averaged left half-sandwich expression.** Let $\psi$ be the two-register state, let $F$ be the indexed polynomial family, and let $k,\ell$ be natural numbers. Set $n=k-(\ell+1)$. Let $\mathcal U$ be the uniform distribution on a field point and an $n$-tuple. For a sample $(x,z)$ and outcomes $g,h$, write $S$, $U$, and $T$ for the recurrence weight, indexed outcome effect, and half-product operator from the formal statement. Then
--
--   $$
--   \mathcal M_1
--   =\mathbb E_{(x,z)\sim\mathcal U}\sum_{g,h}\operatorname{ev}_\psi\!\left(
--   \operatorname{leftTensor}(UT)\left(\operatorname{leftTensor}(T^\dagger)\operatorname{rightTensor}(SU)\right)\right),
--   $$
--
--   where $\mathcal M_1$ denotes the formal `fromHToGAdjacentStageM1` quantity. The global identity applies the pointwise $M_1$ left half-sandwich rewrite under the uniform average and feeds `fromHToGAdjacentStage_paperMoveChain`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToGAdjacentStageM1_eq_halfSandwichLeftShape`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
